{#
mail/_message_body.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
One message body, and everything that has to be true around it.

Included from the conversation view, the single-message pane and the trust
Turbo Stream — so it owns the id those three agree on.

WHY THE BODY IS IN AN IFRAME
────────────────────────────
It used to be injected straight into the app's own DOM. MailBodySanitizer held
— nothing got through it — but "the sanitizer has no gaps" is a claim that has
to keep being true forever, against every sender, and the cost of it being
wrong once was a same-origin script with the session cookie. In here a gap is
worth nothing: no allow-same-origin means an opaque origin, which has no access
to our cookies, our storage or this document. The second thing it buys is
smaller but hits every day — a sender's `td { padding: 0 }` can no longer
reach the application's own layout.

WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *OUTSIDE* THE FRAME
────────────────────────────────────────
Every warning, and the images bar. A banner rendered inside the sandbox is a
banner mail markup can draw for itself, and a "Show images" button the message
can forge is worse than no button at all. The trust boundary and the visual
boundary are the same line.

Variables:
  message  Message
#}
{% set render = message_render(message) %}
{# Sent, and not gone yet: the browser built the message, and until the send
   job has handed it over there is nothing here to read. The draft is sealed,
   or the body was blanked because only the recipients may read it, and the
   raw source — the bytes that went out — does not exist until they have gone.
   Shown as being sent, not as a draft and not as something to decrypt: asking
   the keyring for a source that is not there yet is how a reply to encrypted
   mail came to say the keys were locked. The worker's outcome stream swaps
   the whole message for its sent self once it has gone (see
   mail/_send_outcome.stream.html.twig). outgoingSeal rather than sentAt: it
   is cleared in the same flush that stores the raw source, and sentAt is
   written before either. #}
{% set sendingSealed = message.outgoingSeal is not null
    and (message.sealedDraft or (message.outgoingSeal.kind ?? null) == 'encrypted') %}
{# A draft sealed in the browser has no raw source to decrypt: it is opened in
   the composer, never here. See App\Service\Crypto\SealedDrafts. #}
{% set sealedDraft = message.sealedDraft and not sendingSealed %}
{# A decrypted body a browser handed over (DecryptedMail) is shown like any
   body the server holds; only the banner says where it came from. #}
{% set decryptedKept = message.plaintextSource.value == 'client' %}
{# Opened in the browser: OpenPGP always — every person has address keys —
   and S/MIME once the person has a certificate of their own to open it with
   (phase 6c of #28). Without one, S/MIME is only said to be unreadable. #}
{% set encryptedHere = not sendingSealed and not sealedDraft and not decryptedKept and message.crypto is not null and message.crypto.encrypted %}
{% set encryptedInBrowser = encryptedHere and (message.crypto.pgp or has_smime_certificate()) %}

<div id="message_body_{{ message.id }}" class="mail-message-body">

    {# ── Warnings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% if render.inSpam %}
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-danger/40 bg-danger/10 px-3 py-2.5 mb-3"
             data-testid="spam-warning">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation text-danger mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-danger">{{ 'message.security.spam.title'|trans }}</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted">{{ 'message.security.spam.body'|trans }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if render.mismatch is not null %}
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-warning/40 bg-warning/10 px-3 py-2.5 mb-3"
             data-testid="sender-mismatch-warning">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield text-warning mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'message.security.mismatch.title'|trans }}</p>
                {# Shows its working: the claim, and the address it came from.
                   A reader can disagree with a fact; they can only obey a verdict. #}
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted break-words">
                    {{ render.mismatch.kind.translationKey|trans({
                        '%claimed%': render.mismatch.claimed,
                        '%actual%':  render.mismatch.actual,
                    }) }}
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── The images bar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# ABOVE the frame, with the warnings, and below the attachment chips the
       thread template draws before this include.

       It used to sit under the body, which put it past the fold on anything
       longer than a screen: the reader met a message full of gaps, scrolled to
       the end to find out why, then scrolled back. The bar is not a footnote
       about what happened — it is the control for reading the message at all,
       so it belongs where the decision is made, before the reading starts.

       Still outside the frame, which is the part that is not negotiable: a
       "Show images" button the message could draw for itself is worse than no
       button. #}
    {% if render.offersImages %}
        <div
            class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1.5 mb-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-raised px-3 py-2"
            data-testid="images-bar"
            data-controller="mail--remote-images"
        >
            <i class="fa-regular fa-image text-ink-faint text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="text-xs text-ink-muted flex-1 min-w-0">
                {{ 'message.images.blocked'|trans({'%count%': render.content.blocked}) }}
            </span>

            <button
                type="button"
                data-action="click->mail--remote-images#show"
                data-testid="show-images"
                class="text-xs font-medium text-link hover:underline"
            >{{ 'message.images.show_once'|trans }}</button>

            {# Only offered where it can be honoured. A message in Spam does not
               load images on an allowlist (see MessageRenderer), so offering to
               add one here would be a button that visibly does nothing. #}
            {% if not render.inSpam %}
                <form
                    method="post"
                    action="{{ path('app_mail_images_trust', {'id': message.id}) }}"
                    data-turbo="true"
                >
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('images-trust' ~ message.id) }}">
                    <button
                        type="submit"
                        data-testid="always-show-images"
                        class="text-xs font-medium text-link hover:underline"
                    >{{ 'message.images.always'|trans({'%sender%': message.fromAddress}) }}</button>
                </form>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── OpenPGP and S/MIME ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# The banner, and for an encrypted message the whole body: the server
       holds none, so the browser decrypts the raw source — OpenPGP or S/MIME
       — and fills the same frame the branch below would have
       (mail--encrypted-message). The frame document is rendered here with a
       placeholder for the body, so both paths show a message in exactly the
       same document. #}
    {% if sendingSealed %}
        <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-ink-muted" data-testid="sending-encrypted" data-sending-sealed>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-lock text-success text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'message.crypto.sending'|trans }}
        </p>
    {% elseif sealedDraft %}
        <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-ink-muted" data-testid="sealed-draft-note">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-lock text-success text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'message.crypto.sealed_draft'|trans }}
        </p>
    {% elseif encryptedInBrowser %}
        {% set frameDocument %}{% include 'mail/_frame_document.html.twig' with { render: render, body: '<!--plmail:body-->' } only %}{% endset %}
        <div data-controller="mail--encrypted-message"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-outer-subject-value="{{ message.subject }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-raw-url-value="{{ path('app_mail_message_raw', { id: message.id }) }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-upload-url-value="{{ keeps_decrypted(message.account) ? path('app_mail_decrypted_upload', { id: message.id }) : '' }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-sender-keys-url-value="{{ path('app_contact_keys_sender', { email: message.fromAddress }) }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-smime-signer-url-value="{{ message.crypto.pgp ? '' : path('app_contact_keys_message_smime_signer', { id: message.id }) }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-document-value="{{ frameDocument|e('html') }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-settings-url-value="{{ path('app_settings_index', { section: 'encryption' }) }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-keyring-value="{{ {
                 stateUrl:    path('app_keyring_state'),
                 unlockUrl:   path('app_keyring_unlock_current'),
                 preloginUrl: path('app_login_prelogin'),
                 csrf:        csrf_token('keyring'),
                 userId:      app.user.id,
                 email:       app.user.email,
             }|json_encode }}"
             data-mail--encrypted-message-messages-value="{{ {
                 decrypting:    'message.crypto.decrypting'|trans,
                 locked:        'message.crypto.locked'|trans,
                 openSettings:  'message.crypto.open_settings'|trans,
                 noKey:         'message.crypto.no_key'|trans,
                 noCertificate: 'message.crypto.smime_unreadable'|trans,
                 unsupported:   'message.crypto.smime_unsupported'|trans,
                 noSource:      'message.crypto.no_source'|trans,
                 failed:        'message.crypto.failed'|trans,
                 subject:       'message.crypto.subject'|trans({ '%subject%': '%subject%' }),
                 signature: {
                     valid:       'message.crypto.inner.valid'|trans,
                     invalid:     'message.crypto.inner.invalid'|trans,
                     unknown_key: 'message.crypto.inner.unknown_key'|trans,
                     untrusted:   'message.crypto.inner.untrusted'|trans,
                     key_changed: 'message.crypto.inner.key_changed'|trans,
                     unchecked:   'message.crypto.inner.unchecked'|trans,
                 },
                 attachedKey: {
                     heading:     'message.crypto.attached_key.heading'|trans,
                     own:         'message.crypto.attached_key.own'|trans,
                     keep:        'message.crypto.attached_key.keep'|trans,
                     accept:      'message.crypto.attached_key.accept'|trans,
                     noneHint:    'message.crypto.attached_key.none_hint'|trans,
                     changedHint: 'message.crypto.attached_key.changed_hint'|trans,
                 },
             }|json_encode }}">
            {% include 'mail/_crypto_banner.html.twig' with { message: message } only %}

            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted" data-mail--encrypted-message-target="status" role="status">
                {{ 'message.crypto.decrypting'|trans }}
            </p>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-3" data-mail--encrypted-message-target="attachments" hidden></div>

            <div data-controller="mail--message-frame"
                 data-mail--message-frame-min-height-value="80"
                 data-mail--encrypted-message-target="frameHost"
                 class="relative"
                 hidden>
                <iframe data-mail--message-frame-target="frame"
                        data-mail--encrypted-message-target="frame"
                        aria-label="{{ 'message.body_frame'|trans }}"
                        sandbox="{{ render.sandbox }}"
                        referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
                        class="w-full block border-0 bg-transparent"
                        style="height: 80px;"></iframe>
                <div data-mail--message-frame-target="status"
                     class="hidden absolute bottom-0 left-0 max-w-full truncate rounded-tr-md bg-ink/85 text-inverse-ink px-2 py-1 text-[11px] font-mono pointer-events-none z-10"></div>
            </div>

            <pre class="mail-sheet whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-sans text-sm" data-mail--encrypted-message-target="text" hidden></pre>
        </div>
    {% elseif message.crypto is not null or attached_sender_key(message) is not null %}
        {# Also for a plain message that only carries its sender's key: the
           banner is where that key is said, since it is no longer listed
           among the attachments. #}
        {% include 'mail/_crypto_banner.html.twig' with { message: message } only %}

        {% if encryptedHere %}
            {# S/MIME, and the person has no certificate of their own to open
               it with: nothing for the browser to try. #}
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted" data-testid="smime-unreadable">{{ 'message.crypto.smime_unreadable'|trans }}</p>
        {% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    {# ── The reading frame ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% if encryptedHere or sealedDraft or sendingSealed %}
        {# Drawn above, by the browser — or, for a sealed draft and a message
           still being sent, not at all. #}
    {% elseif render.content.html is not empty %}

        {% set frameDocument %}{% include 'mail/_frame_document.html.twig' with { render: render, body: render.content.html } only %}{% endset %}

        <div
            data-controller="mail--message-frame"
            data-mail--message-frame-min-height-value="80"
            class="relative"
        >
            <iframe
                data-mail--message-frame-target="frame"
                {# aria-label, not title: the frame still needs an accessible
                   name, but `title` on an iframe is also a browser tooltip, so
                   it popped up "Message content" over the whole body on every
                   hover. aria-label names it for assistive tech and shows
                   nothing on hover. #}
                aria-label="{{ 'message.body_frame'|trans }}"
                sandbox="{{ render.sandbox }}"
                referrerpolicy="no-referrer"
                loading="lazy"
                class="w-full block border-0 bg-transparent"
                style="height: 80px;"
                srcdoc="{{ frameDocument|e('html') }}"
            ></iframe>

            {# The link preview. In the parent, pinned to the frame's corner —
               it reads as part of the frame and cannot be drawn by the mail. #}
            <div
                data-mail--message-frame-target="status"
                class="hidden absolute bottom-0 left-0 max-w-full truncate rounded-tr-md bg-ink/85 text-inverse-ink px-2 py-1 text-[11px] font-mono pointer-events-none z-10"
                data-testid="link-preview"
            ></div>
        </div>
    {% elseif render.text %}
        {# No HTML body: plain text needs no sandbox, because there is no markup
           to sandbox. Twig escapes it, so it is text all the way down. #}
        <pre class="mail-sheet whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-sans text-sm">{{ render.text }}</pre>
    {% endif %}

    {% if render.senderTrusted and render.content.allowed > 0 %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3 text-xs text-ink-faint" data-testid="images-trusted">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-check text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate">
                {{ 'message.images.trusted'|trans({'%sender%': message.fromAddress}) }}
            </span>
            <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_mail_images_distrust', {'id': message.id}) }}" data-turbo="true">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('images-distrust' ~ message.id) }}">
                <button type="submit" class="font-medium text-link hover:underline">
                    {{ 'message.images.stop_trusting'|trans }}
                </button>
            </form>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

</div>
